## 4. Household duplicate detection & shared household id

The "what is a household" definition is single-sourced in:

**`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/HouseholdKey.java`**
```java
package org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.function.owner;

import java.util.Locale;
import java.util.Objects;

import org.springframework.samples.petclinic.model.Owner;

final class HouseholdKey {

    private final String lastName;
    private final String address;

    private HouseholdKey(String lastName, String address) {
        this.lastName = lastName;
        this.address = address;
    }

    static HouseholdKey of(Owner owner) {
        return new HouseholdKey(normalize(owner.getLastName()), normalize(owner.getAddress()));
    }

    boolean matches(Owner owner) {
        return equals(of(owner));
    }

    String canonical() {
        return lastName + "|" + address;
    }

    @Override public boolean equals(Object o) {
        if (this == o) return true;
        if (!(o instanceof HouseholdKey other)) return false;
        return lastName.equals(other.lastName) && address.equals(other.address);
    }

    @Override public int hashCode() { return Objects.hash(lastName, address); }
    @Override public String toString() { return canonical(); }

    private static String normalize(String value) {
        if (value == null) return "";
        return value.trim().replaceAll("\\s+", " ").toLowerCase(Locale.ROOT);
    }
}
```
A household = same `lastName` + same `address`, normalized (trim, collapse whitespace, lowercase).

